## 🎉 Rotating Card – Hover‑to‑Rotate Demo

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body{
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  min-height:100vh;
  margin:0;
  background:#f0f0f0;
  font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card container ---------- */
.card{
  width:260px;
  height:160px;
  perspective:800px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  cursor:pointer;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Card inner (the part that actually rotates) ---------- */
.card__inner{
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  position:relative;
  transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
  transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card__face{
  position:absolute;
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  backface-visibility:hidden;       /* hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius:12px;
  box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  font-size:1.2rem;
  color:#fff;
}

.card__face--front{
  background:#4a90e2;
}

.card__face--back{
  background:#e94e77;
  transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* place it behind the front face */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣  Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card__inner{
  transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* flip the card */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card__inner">
    <div class="card__face card__face--front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card__face card__face--back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | CSS |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | The page is centered and given a light background. | `display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center;` |
| 2 | `.card` sets a **perspective** so the 3D rotation looks realistic. | `perspective:800px;` |
| 3 | `.card__inner` is the element that actually rotates. It has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its children stay in 3D space. | `transform-style:preserve-3d;` |
| 4 | Two faces (`front` and `back`) are absolutely positioned on top of each other. The back face is rotated 180° so it sits behind the front. | `backface-visibility:hidden;` + `transform:rotateY(180deg);` |
| 5 | On hover, the inner wrapper rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, flipping the card. | `transform:rotateY(180deg);` |

### Tweaks & Variations

| Want to change? | How to do it |
|-----------------|--------------|
| Rotate around X‑axis instead of Y | Replace `rotateY(180deg)` with `rotateX(180deg)` |
| Flip only on click | Add a small JS snippet that toggles a class on click instead of using `:hover`. |
| Add more content | Put any HTML inside `.card__face--front` or `.card__face--back`. |
| Different animation speed | Change `transition:transform 0.6s ease;` to another duration or easing. |

Enjoy experimenting! 🚀
